-- title:
--   Matching a_ℓ(g) with Frobenius traces of a Weierstrass model
-- statement:
--   Fix $M \in \mathbb{N}$ nonzero, a weight-two cusp form $g$ for $\Gamma_0(M)$, a finite set $S \subseteq \mathbb{N}$, and a ring homomorphism $\chi_g$ from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) — the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(M)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid M$, $\ell \notin S$, together with $U_q$ for primes $q \mid M$, $q \notin S$ — to $\mathbb{C}$, such that $\chi_g(T_\ell)$ equals the $\ell$-th coefficient of the $q$-expansion of $g$ (width $1$) for every prime $\ell \nmid M$ with $\ell \notin S$. Let $O'$ be a commutative local ring of characteristic zero, $\iota$ an injective ring homomorphism from the range of $\chi_g$ into $O'$, $W$ a Weierstrass curve over $\mathbb{Z}$, and $\rho$ a [`GaloisRepAdic O'`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L16), i.e. a rank-two finite free $O'$-module $V$ with a monoid homomorphism $\rho$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ (as $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphisms of $\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb{Q}$) to $\operatorname{End}_{O'}(V)$ satisfying the adic continuity condition. Assume two hypotheses about characteristic polynomials of $\rho(\sigma)$ for valuation subrings $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell \in A^{\mathrm{nonunits}}$ and $\sigma$ in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ acting as $x \mapsto x^\ell$ on the residue field of $A$: for all primes $\ell \nmid M$ with $\ell \notin S$ it is $X^2 - \iota(\chi_g(T_\ell)) X + \ell$, and for all primes $\ell \notin S$ with $\ell \nmid \Delta(W)$ in $\mathbb{Z}$ it is $X^2 - a_\ell(W) X + \ell$, where $a_\ell(W) = \ell + 1 - \#(W \bmod \ell)$ is the Frobenius trace of the reduction of $W$ modulo $\ell$. The conclusion: for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid \Delta(W)$, $\ell \nmid M$ and $\ell \notin S$, the $\ell$-th $q$-expansion coefficient of $g$ equals $a_\ell(W)$ in $\mathbb{C}$.
--
--   This is the comparison step which converts an identification of two-dimensional $\lambda$-adic Galois representations into the numerical Eichler–Shimura identity $a_\ell(g) = a_\ell(W)$ at good primes away from $M$ and from the excluded set $S$, the form in which modularity of a Weierstrass model is recorded. It is used in the assembly of [`WeierstrassCurve.isModularModelOfLevel_conductorLevel_of_not_cube_dvd_of_modRepIsIrreducible_of_factorization_eq`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.isModularModelOfLevel_conductorLevel_of_not_cube_dvd_of_modRepIsIrreducible_of_factorization_eq).
